#==============================================================================================
#
#   readable_stream_operations_1 - the abstract operations of readable streams and their
#   default readers: acquiring, creating, teeing a byte stream, canceling, closing, erroring,
#   reading
#
#   DESCRIPTION:
#       Port of Libraries/LibWeb/Streams/ReadableStreamOperations.cpp (lines 56-1258), as part
#       of the ReadableStream stand-in of DESIGN.md §3.6 (region p2s): the operations of byte
#       streams read by default readers. Default controllers (ReadableStreamDefaultTee,
#       CreateReadableStream), BYOB readers and read-into requests, piping and streams from
#       iterables are phase 4; a path that reaches one traps.
#
#       Where a ReadableStream member has the snake name of an abstract operation (close,
#       error, tee, cancel; ReadableStreamDefaultReader's read), the member keeps the name and
#       the operation takes `_2`, as the skeleton generator names a later declaration
#       (DESIGN.md §4.2).
